    {
      "id": "7zoerv8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11.1 Temples – The 'Temple City'"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Kalinga Architecture represents a distinct regional sub-style of Nagara temple architecture found across Odisha.",
        "Bhubaneswar is historically revered as the 'Temple City' owing to its vast concentration of ancient temples.",
        "Odissi is one of the eight classical dance forms of India, deeply rooted in Odisha's temple traditions and Mahari practices.",
        "The state's heritage encompasses vibrant folk dances, traditional crafts, rich textiles, unique literary history, and UNESCO World Heritage Sites."
      ],
      "id": "096jkdh"
    },
